  "response": "I’m using the repository’s crimes codebase-risk workflow to inspect the four reported form subtrees and ground the proposed component API in their actual differences.\n\nThe finding is specifically the footer/action row, not the customer, amount, or status fields: the repeated `<div>` contains the fixed Cancel link and a submit button whose label differs between create and edit. I’m checking the two dashboard app boundaries before choosing whether this should be one physical module or one component per independently built example.\n\nFinding `crime_00070` identifies the repeated invoice-form action footer:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link href=\"/dashboard/invoices\">Cancel</Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create/Edit Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nExtract `InvoiceFormActions`, keeping submit behavior composable:\n\n```tsx\ntype InvoiceFormActionsProps = {\n  cancelHref?: string;        // defaults to \"/dashboard/invoices\"\n  cancelLabel?: ReactNode;    // defaults to \"Cancel\"\n  children: ReactNode;        // primary-action slot\n};\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Edit Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\nThe `children` slot lets forms later supply pending-state buttons or additional submit behavior without duplicating the layout and Cancel-link styling.\n\nFiles to change:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n\nBecause `final-example` and `starter-example` are independent Next.js applications with app-local `@/*` aliases, each should receive an app-local module:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n\nBoth modules should expose the same `InvoiceFormActions` API. A single physical cross-app module would require introducing a shared workspace package and changing both build configurations—too broad for this small refactor.",
